# A pipeline in parentheses or in a call argument without `from`: one DS0150 each, and none for the query that starts with the parenthesized pipeline.
mode: syntax
---- query
(orders | where amount > 1) | take 5;
from t | extend n = f(u | count)
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..71
  PIPELINE@0..36
    PAREN_EXPR@0..27
      L_PAREN@0..1 "("
      PIPELINE@1..26
        NAME_REF@1..7
          IDENT@1..7 "orders"
        WHITESPACE@7..8 " "
        PIPE@8..9 "|"
        WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
        WHERE_OP@10..26
          IDENT@10..15 "where"
          WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
          BIN_EXPR@16..26
            NAME_REF@16..22
              IDENT@16..22 "amount"
            WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
            GT@23..24 ">"
            WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
            LITERAL@25..26
              LONG@25..26 "1"
      R_PAREN@26..27 ")"
    WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
    PIPE@28..29 "|"
    WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
    TAKE_OP@30..36
      IDENT@30..34 "take"
      WHITESPACE@34..35 " "
      LITERAL@35..36
        LONG@35..36 "5"
  SEMICOLON@36..37 ";"
  WHITESPACE@37..38 "\n"
  PIPELINE@38..70
    IDENT@38..42 "from"
    WHITESPACE@42..43 " "
    NAME_REF@43..44
      IDENT@43..44 "t"
    WHITESPACE@44..45 " "
    PIPE@45..46 "|"
    WHITESPACE@46..47 " "
    EXTEND_OP@47..70
      IDENT@47..53 "extend"
      WHITESPACE@53..54 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@54..70
        NAME@54..55
          IDENT@54..55 "n"
        WHITESPACE@55..56 " "
        EQ@56..57 "="
        WHITESPACE@57..58 " "
        CALL_EXPR@58..70
          NAME_REF@58..59
            IDENT@58..59 "f"
          ARG_LIST@59..70
            L_PAREN@59..60 "("
            PIPELINE@60..69
              NAME_REF@60..61
                IDENT@60..61 "u"
              WHITESPACE@61..62 " "
              PIPE@62..63 "|"
              WHITESPACE@63..64 " "
              COUNT_OP@64..69
                IDENT@64..69 "count"
            R_PAREN@69..70 ")"
  WHITESPACE@70..71 "\n"

error[DS0150]: a pipeline starts with `from`
  --> query:1:2
  |
1 | (orders | where amount > 1) | take 5;
  |  ^^^^^^ this table needs `from` before it
  |
  = help: insert `from`: `from orders`

error[DS0150]: a pipeline starts with `from`
  --> query:2:23
  |
2 | from t | extend n = f(u | count)
  |                       ^ this table needs `from` before it
  |
  = help: insert `from`: `from u`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    (from orders | where amount > 1) | take 5;
    from t | extend n = f(from u | count)
which parses without errors
